[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m disjuncts each that are listed separately). There are **no** `assert`s, **no**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m error enums, **no** `RETURN_ERROR`-style macros, and **no** `errno` use in this
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m library.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Reachability note (important, and itself verified)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `memchra2` is the **only** exported symbol. Its signature is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `int memchra2(int, int, int, int)` — four by-value `int`s. Consequently:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * There is **no pointer parameter**, so no caller-supplied null pointer can
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   reach any of the `NULL` guards.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * There is **no length/size parameter**, so no caller-supplied zero or
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   oversized length can reach any of the size guards.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * There is **no enum parameter**, so there is no out-of-range-enum input class.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Every buffer, array, and count the helpers see is constructed **internally**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   by `memchra2` with fixed shapes (`char buffer[64]`, `int values[4]`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `char *test_strings[4]`, `unsigned char bytes[4]`, count/len literals `4`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So each row below records both the trigger and whether an external caller can
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reach it. Rows marked *unreachable* are still tested: the differential test
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m asserts that C and Rust agree on the **branch outcome the guard produces for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the internally-constructed input** (i.e. that both take the same side of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m guard), which is the only externally observable consequence. Rows marked
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *reachable* are driven directly from `memchra2`'s four `int` arguments.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## The table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | reachable from public API? | test |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|---------------------------|------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `process_buffer` | `buffer == NULL` | `return -1` | no — caller always passes `char buffer[64]` (never null) | `err_row01_process_buffer_null_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `process_buffer` | `*buffer == '\0'` (empty string) | `return -1` | no — buffer always starts with `'t'` of `"test"` | `err_row02_process_buffer_empty_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `process_strings` | `strings == NULL` | `return 0` | no — caller passes a 4-element literal array | `err_row03_process_strings_null_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `process_strings` | `count <= 0` | `return 0` | no — caller passes literal `4` | `err_row04_process_strings_count_le_zero_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | `process_strings` | element `*i == NULL` | `continue` (element skipped, not counted) | no — all 4 literals are non-null | `err_row05_process_strings_null_element_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `process_strings` | element `**i == '\0'` (empty string element) | `continue` (element skipped, not counted) | no — all 4 literals are non-empty | `err_row06_process_strings_empty_element_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 7 | `safe_sum_array` | `arr == NULL` | `return 0` | no — caller passes `int values[4]` | `err_row07_safe_sum_array_null_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 8 | `safe_sum_array` | `size == 0` | `return 0` | no — caller passes literal `4` | `err_row08_safe_sum_array_zero_size_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 9 | `interpret_as_int` | `bytes == NULL` | `return 0` | no — caller passes `unsigned char bytes[4]` | `err_row09_interpret_as_int_null_unreachable` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 10 | `interpret_as_int` | `len < sizeof(int)` (i.e. `len < 4`) | `return 0` | no — caller passes literal `4`, and `sizeof(int) == 4` on the reference platform | `err_row10_interpret_as_int_short_len_unreachable` |
