[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 17 | `memchra2` | `buf_sum > 0` fails, i.e. `process_buffer` returned `-1` or a non-positive sum | the `result += buf_sum % 256` contribution is **skipped** | no — the buffer always contains printable ASCII with positive `(int)(char)` values and a non-empty first byte, so `buf_sum > 0` always holds | `err_row17_buf_sum_always_positive` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Generic FFI-boundary boundary cases (mandated even though absent from the table)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `memchra2` takes no pointers, no lengths, and no enums, so the classic
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m null-pointer / zero-length / oversized-length / out-of-range-enum inputs have
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **no parameter to occupy**. The corresponding boundary class for a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4×`int` signature is the extremes and one-step-past values of `int` itself,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m plus the `unsigned int`/`char`/`float` reinterpretations the body performs.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m These are covered by:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | boundary class | test |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------------|------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G1 | `INT_MIN` / `INT_MAX` in every argument position, and all 4^4 combinations of them | `boundary_int_extremes_cross_product` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G2 | one step past the extremes (`INT_MIN+1`, `INT_MAX-1`) and around zero (`-1`, `0`, `1`) | `boundary_one_step_past` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G3 | signed-overflow of `a+b+c+d` in `safe_sum_array` (C wraps at `-O0`; Rust must wrap identically) | `boundary_sum_overflow` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G4 | low-byte extraction extremes (`x & 0xFF` == `0x00` and `0xFF`) feeding `interpret_as_int` and `complex_iteration` | `boundary_low_byte_extremes` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G5 | `(char)c` sign-extension boundary in `memchra` / `count_occurrences` (byte `0x80`, `0x7F`, `0xFF`) | `boundary_char_sign_extension` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G6 | every IEEE-754 class of `a` reinterpreted as `float`: ±0, subnormal, normal, ±inf, quiet/signalling NaN, and the exact `1000.0f` cut point ±1 ulp | `boundary_ieee754_classes` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | G7 | "out-of-range value with no valid variant" analogue: every `a` whose float reinterpretation has no meaningful numeric value (all 2^23 NaN payloads sampled) | `boundary_nan_payloads` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
