[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Public entry points
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/include/lib.h` declares exactly one:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m int memchra2(int a, int b, int c, int d);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are no convenience-vs-low-level tiers to choose between: `memchra2` *is*
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the lowest-level public entry point, and it is the only one. The 8 helpers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`memchra`, `process_buffer`, `int_to_float_bits`, `process_strings`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `safe_sum_array`, `interpret_as_int`, `count_occurrences`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `complex_iteration`) are `static`, so they are not part of the linkable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m surface — they are reachable only through `memchra2`, and every row below
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m drives the whole composed pipeline end to end through it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Runtime options / modes / flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Grep census: the C source contains **no** `#ifdef`, **no** `#if`, **no**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `switch`, no global/`static` mutable state, no setter functions, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m environment-variable reads, and no configuration struct.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m $ grep -c '#ifdef\|#if \|switch\|setenv\|getenv\|static [a-z_]* [a-z_]* =' c_src/src/lib.c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 0
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `memchra2` is therefore a pure function of its four `int` arguments, and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "configuration" axes are exactly the input **shapes** the body branches on.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is likewise no `[features]` table in `translation/Cargo.toml`, so there is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m one build configuration.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 1 — IEEE-754 class of `a`** (from `int_to_float_bits(a)` and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `if (f > 0.0f && f < 1000.0f)` test). Seven classes the branch distinguishes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | class | `a` (as `uint32`) | `f` | branch | contribution |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-------|-------------------|-----|--------|--------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `Zero` | `0x00000000` | `+0.0` | not taken | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `PosSubnormal` | `0x00000001` … `0x007FFFFF` | `0 < f < 2^-126` | taken | `(int)f == 0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `PosNormLtOne` | `0x00800000` … `0x3F7FFFFF` | `2^-126 <= f < 1.0` | taken | `(int)f == 0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `PosNormInRange` | `0x3F800000` … `0x4479FFFF` | `1.0 <= f < 1000.0` | taken | `(int)f` ∈ `[1, 999]` |
